===Prelude and first years of the Boreal War ({{abbr|2329|1935 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}–{{abbr|2332|1937 (Earth Year Equivalent)}})===
{{Main|Boreal War}}

*{{abbr|2329|1934.76 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: ENEMY declares war against Qym and co, and invades ALLY. Bacha XV makes a speech indicating total support as part of the [[Nagur Pact]]. Most of the initial fighting occurs in ALLY. 
*{{abbr|2330|1935.59 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: ENEMY is pushed back but maintains a stronghold in invaded ALLY. 
*{{abbr|2331|1936.42 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Qym reluctant to send more troops and material. Enemy reluctant to advance more, vulnerable to other fronts. 
*{{abbr|2332|1937.25 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Bacha XV automatically abdicates the throne, per Qymish law.

==Sixteenth Bachan era ({{abbr|2332|1937 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}–{{abbr|2372|1970 (Earth Year Equivalent)}})==
{{Main|Sixteenth Bachan era}}

===Lull of the Boreal War ({{abbr|2332|1937 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}–{{abbr|2334|1939 (Earth Year Equivalent)}})===
{{Main|Boreal War}}

*{{abbr|2332|1937.25 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Bacha XVI takes over and continues the war. 
*{{abbr|2333|1938 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Peace overtures begin, with informal contacts and reduced military actions. Qym secretly prepares military and industrial buildup. 
*{{abbr|2334|1938.9 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Establishment of the [[Basis Forum]] in order to facilitate diplomatic exchanges between the two warring sides. 

===Total Boreal War ({{abbr|2334|1939 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}–{{abbr|2340|1944 (Earth Year Equivalent)}})===
{{Main|Boreal War}}

*{{abbr|2334|1938.90 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Negotiations collapse due to mistrust after Qymish and Enemy buildups revealed. 
*{{abbr|2335|1939.74 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: War intensifies with surprise attacks. War aims change on both sides. Other countries join in. 
*{{abbr|2336|1940.58 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Total war begins with military industrial focus. Multiple fronts open. 
*{{abbr|2337|1941.41 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Zhol and other Qymish cities are heavily bombarded. Difficult fight for air supremacy. Nagur Pact is renewed. 
*{{abbr|2338|1942.24 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Enemy conquers Ally and pushes into Qym, invading the [[March of Rumyk]]. Beginning of the [[Battle of Teurek]]. 
*{{abbr|2339|1943.07 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: End of the [[Battle of Teurek]], Qym pushes back with a counter-offensive. Liberates Ally. 
*{{abbr|2340|1943.90 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Qym defeats Enemy who surrender. Bacha XVI imposes his peace conditions. 

===Post-war reconstruction ({{abbr|2340|1944 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}–{{abbr|2350|1952.2 (Earth Year Equivalent)}})===
{{Main|Aftermath of the Boreal War}}

*{{abbr|2340|1943.90 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Establishment of the [[Boreal Cooperation Council]] with its headquarters in [[Zhol]]. 
*{{abbr|2341|1944.73 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Establishment of the [[Basis Development Bank]] for post-war reconstruction, with its headquarters in [[Zhol]].
*{{abbr|2342|1945.56 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Qym joins the [[Meranian Diplomatic League]]. 
*{{abbr|2343|1946.39 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Establishment of the [[International Trade Federation]] and the [[Organization of Sukatic Nations]]. 
*{{abbr|2344|1947.22 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Signature of the [[Patsalys Protocols]] prohibiting the development, production, and stockpiling of chemical and biological weapons.
*{{abbr|2345|1948.05 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: End of rationing and the war economy. Full recovery declared by King Bacha XVI. 
*{{abbr|2346|1948.88 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Start of the secret [[Qymish nuclear weapons program]].
*{{abbr|2347|1949.71 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Nagur Pact is renewed. 
*{{abbr|2348|1950.54 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: 
*{{abbr|2349|1951.38 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Entry into force of the [[Patsalys Protocols]].
*{{abbr|2350|1952.21 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}: Qym imposes [[International sanctions against Geno|sanctions against Geno]] due to its chemical and biological weapon programs and continuous human rights violations.

